<title>FRANCE: France pledges 20 billion FFR in state aid for GAN.</title>
<headline>France pledges 20 billion FFR in state aid for GAN.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government has pledged to commit 20 billion francs ($3.5 billion) to state-controlled insurer GAN to shore up its accounts and pave the way for its privatisation, the company said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Some 11 billion francs of the aid would come in the form of a capital injection while nine billion francs would be to cover estimated losses, Groupe des Assurances Nationales (GAN) said in a statement.</p>
<p>($ = 5.694 French Francs)</p>
</text>
